        "--title",
        "comparison launch",
        "The streaming decoder class Inflate (src/inflate.ts) tracks whether the compressed stream has ended in a private `ended` field, and its push(data, flush_mode) method returns a blanket false for every call made after that point. A compressed stream can end before the caller's data does (trailing bytes after the deflate or gzip stream), and the caller has no way to know that in advance, so a push made after the end must become a no-op that reports the recorded outcome instead: once the stream has ended, push returns true if the decode finished without error (this.err is Z_OK) and false if it failed, whatever data or flush mode it is given, and it leaves `err`, `msg` and `result` exactly as they were, so the delivered result survives any trailing chunks and a failed stream keeps reporting failure. Make `ended` a public, documented property so callers can check it, and document the new push behaviour in its JSDoc. Pushes before the end, the onData and onEnd callbacks, the one-shot inflate helpers and everything else are unchanged. The project's full check (npm test: lint, build, type-check and the node test suite) must keep passing; change only src/inflate.ts (a CHANGELOG entry is welcome but not required) and do not edit tests or benchmarks.\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: npm test\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/."
      ],
